EXT. ABANDONED SKATE PARK - NIGHT

Cracked concrete bowls. A chain-link fence sags. Sleet has started, thin and mean, and one flickering streetlight buzzes over the empty ramps.

MAYA, 16, short, braids, a thrifted puffer jacket two sizes too big, stands at the lip of the biggest bowl. Her phone glows in her hand. Screen reads: "grp chat: SURVIVORS (14)". Only one other name is still green.

A shape climbs over the fence. JALEN, 17, tall, a hoodie soaked black, a flashlight in his teeth. He drops it into his palm.

                    JALEN
(waving, shaky)
Okay. So it's us. Everyone else left the chat.

                    MAYA
(not moving)
You're taller than your pfp.

                    JALEN
(laughing, breath fogging)
You're real. Like, actually real.

Her phone BUZZES. A new message from someone neither of them knows: "dont go home."

                    MAYA
(holding up the screen)
Did you send this?

                    JALEN
(reading, stepping back)
No. Maya, no. I only got the group link like an hour ago.

The streetlight DIES. Darkness takes the park, and the sleet sounds louder. Somewhere past the fence a car door SLAMS.

                    MAYA
(whispering, grabbing his sleeve)
Turn the flashlight off.

                    JALEN
(clicking it off, voice cracking)
I thought this would be, like, cute. A meetup.

                    MAYA
(sliding down behind the concrete)
Yeah. Me too.

The phone BUZZES again, brighter in the dark. She covers it with her palm.

                    JALEN
(crouching beside her)
Do you trust me?

                    MAYA
(a beat, then barely)
I trust you more than the chat.

Footsteps crunch on gravel, slow, getting closer.
